{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter","lean:module:Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Finsupp.LinearCombination"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.finrank_homG_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.finrank_homG_regular","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegularHom.lean#L106-L116","doc":"**`dim_k Hom_G(k[G], V) = dim_k V`.**\n\nThis is the multiplicity statement in the form the Wedderburn count needs: paired with the\nSchur orthonormality of `SpechtSchurDiagonal`, `dim Hom_G(k[G], S^μ)` is on one side the\nmultiplicity of `S^μ` in the regular representation, and on the other `dim S^μ`.\n\n`-- Ref: [sagan2001] §1.10 (the regular representation contains each irreducible with\nmultiplicity equal to its dimension).` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.homGRegularEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.homGRegularEquiv","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegularHom.lean#L78-L104","doc":"**An equivariant map out of the regular representation is its value at `[1]`.**\n`Hom_G(k[G], V) ≃ₗ[k] V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.ofVector_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.ofVector_mem","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegularHom.lean#L66-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.ofVector_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.ofVector_single","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegularHom.lean#L62-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.ofVector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.ofVector","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegularHom.lean#L56-L60","doc":"The inverse construction: a vector `v` determines the equivariant map\n`Σ_g c_g·[g] ↦ Σ_g c_g·(ρ g v)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.evalOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.evalOne","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegularHom.lean#L49-L54","doc":"Evaluation of an equivariant map at the identity basis vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.regular_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.regular_single","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegularHom.lean#L43-L47","doc":"`ρ_reg g` sends the basis vector at `h` to the basis vector at `g * h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RegularHom.regular","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegularHom.lean#L37-L41","doc":"The regular representation of `G` on `G →₀ k`, i.e. `Representation.ofMulAction`\napplied to `G` acting on itself. ","signatureChunk":0}]}